summary:
Today, I came across my old notes from German class and decided to practice stylistic devices (dt. &ldquo;Stilmittel&rdquo;) again. To optimize retention, I built a custom Anki card template utilizing three fields: Name, Definition, and Example. This guide demonstrates how to configure multi-field templates in Anki with automatic cross-learning:
Given Name $\rightarrow$ recall Definition and Example Given Definition $\rightarrow$ recall Name and Example Given Example $\rightarrow$ recall Name and Definition Interactive 3D Flashcard Preview (Click to Flip) 💡 Flashcard ↻ Click or tap to flip Rhetorical Device: Alliteration ✓ Answer / Details ↻ Flip back Definition: Repetition of the same initial consonant sound in consecutive words.
Example: &ldquo;Peter Piper picked a peck of pickled peppers.&rdquo;
